mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Backend API\n\nMinimal Caffeine starter backend. This canister exposes only the base scaffolding needed for the app to run: shared authorization and an empty OQL query surface. There are no business entities or data operations yet.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nThis app uses Internet Identity. The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n## Authorization\n\nAccess is role-based. The first caller to initialize access control becomes the admin; subsequent callers receive the default (non-admin) role. Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, so a principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\n## Methods\n\n### `_initialize_access_control`\n\nInitializes the access-control state. Call once as a signed-in caller before any role-guarded call. The first initializer receives the admin role; later callers receive the default role.\n\n### `getApiDoc`\n\nReturns this document as Markdown. Read-only query; no authentication required.\n\n### `schema` and `execute`\n\nOQL query surface. `schema` returns the queryable schema; `execute` runs a JSON query against it. This starter exposes no entities, so queries return no rows.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\nTimestamps, when introduced, are signed `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch. Identifiers and counters are `Nat`. Optional values are Candid `opt`; variants are Candid variants.\n\n## Errors and limits\n\nRole-guarded endpoints trap for an unregistered or unauthorized caller. There are no destructive or state-mutating business endpoints in this starter."
  };
};
